<section class="retreat-section retreat-details">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>Meals</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Friday dinner, 6:00pm:</strong> taco bar, from Linita's Catering in Nunnelly</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday breakfast, 8:00–10:00am:</strong> breakfast bar with bacon and sausage, from Linita's. Come down any time in the window.</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday lunch, 12:50pm:</strong> loaded baked potato bar, from Linita's</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday dinner, 6:40pm:</strong> Southern dinner from Purdie's Catering: maple mustard glazed chicken and pot roast with gravy, smashed potatoes, green beans, balsamic grilled vegetables, and dessert</li>
      <li><strong>Sunday breakfast, 7:00–8:30am:</strong> a light continental breakfast</li>
      <li><strong>All weekend:</strong> coffee, tea and light snacks</li>
      <li><strong>Dietary needs:</strong> we've passed along the needs you gave us when you registered, and the caterers will set those plates aside and label them. If something has changed, or you didn't tell us, email <a href="mailto:admin@christiantranshumanism.org?subject=CTA%20Retreat%20dietary%20needs">admin@christiantranshumanism.org</a> as soon as you can.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="retreat-section retreat-details">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>What to bring</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bedding and towels are provided</strong> in the lodge. No need to pack sheets or a sleeping bag.</li>
      <li><strong>Clothes in layers:</strong> mid-October evenings in the Tennessee hills get cool, and we'll be outside by the fire both nights.</li>
      <li><strong>Shoes for the outdoors:</strong> sturdy shoes for the trails and the gravel paths. A rain jacket, in case.</li>
      <li><strong>Toiletries</strong> and any medications you need for the weekend.</li>
      <li><strong>A flashlight or headlamp</strong> for the walk back from the fire.</li>
      <li><strong>A water bottle</strong> and a phone charger.</li>
      <li><strong>Something to write in,</strong> and a Bible if you like to have your own.</li>
      <li><strong>An instrument</strong> if you play. There's singing on Saturday afternoon and music by the fire.</li>
      <li><strong>Please leave at home:</strong> alcohol and tobacco. Woodlands is an alcohol- and tobacco-free property.</li>
      <li><strong>Getting in:</strong> the gate code and directions will come to registrants by email before the weekend.</li>
      <li><strong>Questions:</strong> <a href="mailto:admin@christiantranshumanism.org?subject=CTA%20Retreat">admin@christiantranshumanism.org</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

